A||||12||DjKid||Wanting to kill myself, someone help!||||11||
Z||000000||DjKid||08-11-2000||02:51 PM||||Okey, went to wetsand my roof today.. stupid me... wet my windshield wiht it being hot.. *crack* so now.. not a bad crack,  but I was wondering.. how much should I expect to pay for a windshield? can they still be ordered OEM? or is a Boneyard my best bet?<P>------------------<BR>DjKid - 88 Coupe<BR>'Blue Knight"||||reg||11
Z||000001||deceler8||08-11-2000||02:54 PM||||A glass shop might install one for a lot less than you think as long as you're clear that this is being paid out of your own pocket...I've heard of new windshields being installed for $150 or less.<P>Glass places have been known to pad bills when insurance is paying.<P>As to glass from a boneyard, $25 tops (and they pull it).<P>------------------<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/deceler8_sig.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000002||mrfiero||08-11-2000||02:55 PM||||D'oh!  That stinks, but I can honestly say I have done the same thing.  <P>You can find windshields for as little as $100, but beware of poor installations.  The norm is around $200-$300.  No matter the cost, make sure it is a reputable shop that has some sort of warranty against defects and/or workmanship.<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000003||Old Lar||08-11-2000||02:57 PM||||Glass claim on insurance?  ||||reg||1
Z||000004||DjKid||08-11-2000||02:58 PM||||the odd thing is, that car was bought as a parts car.. the only reason I wanted it was cuz the windshield was in good shape.. course after I got the car I put it back together, daily driver status .. ooohhh.. unhappy day.. atleast it is getting painted tonight<P>------------------<BR>DjKid - 88 Coupe<BR>'Blue Knight"||||reg||1
Z||000005||HYPTNOTiSE||08-11-2000||03:08 PM||||I work in a bodyshop and i work along with glass guys. The average price with a glass and install is 150 dollars.  I had to replace a front windsheild in my z-24 cavalier(for sale).  I bought a glass from a junkyard for 50 bucks(20-30 is darn cheap and i have a hard time believing that) They sold it to me for 50 cos i work with them all the time, they would have charge me 75.  I removed and installed the windsheild myself one day when the glass guy was by. I used all his materials and did the work myself, it's not rocket science by any means, just get's a little messy.  So i got a new windsheild for 50 bucks, and i used a universal moulding, free. So thats my windsheild story.<BR><P>------------------<BR>       Mike LeCompte<BR>86 Fiero GT 3.2L w/ Nitrous<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.tcac.net/~daddyg/hypsig.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000006||Raydar||08-11-2000||04:08 PM||||If it's getting painted tonight, I would pull out the molding before doing it. If you pull the molding off with fresh paint, there's a chance you might lift the paint.<P>------------------<BR>Raydar<BR>88 Formula T-Top <BR>88 Coupe (ISO big V-6)<P>When I die, I want to go peacefully, in my sleep, like Grandpa.<BR>Not screaming, like the passengers in his car.||||reg||1
Z||000007||whamel||08-11-2000||05:09 PM||||The dealer in Las Vegas told me it would be about $600 to replace my windshield in my '88 coupe.  Then they proceeded to tell me that the car would be going down to the local auto glass guy for the actual work at a cost of about $150-200.  I never got the work done (and the dealership was HORRIBLE - if anybody heard of my problems on the Fiero or Firebird list about 4-5 years ago), but I can only imagine the padding on the price they did there!  <BR>I was very hesitant to do the work myself, but I just did a search on <A HREF="http://www.car-part.com" TARGET=_blank>www.car-part.com</A>  and got prices from $35-$200 for used windshields from junkyards around the country.  My other auto parts search doesn't seem to have front windshields.||||reg||1
Z||000008||Eric_PA||08-11-2000||05:15 PM||||I just had to replace my windshield on my 84. I got it for $30 from a place called Harry's U-pull-it. They pulled it out for me at that price, some sort of special they had going on for the week. Well anyway I found out the hard way that most glass installers will not install used glass. I would check with an installer if you plan to get a used windshield, they may not install it for you. I ended up putting it in myself with help from a friend. It wasn't bad, but was a bit messy.<P>Eric<P>||||reg||1
Z||000009||webbee||08-11-2000||07:53 PM||||If you get new glass from a glass installer make sure that the replacement glass is made in USA. I got a South African made "special". It looked ok and was safty but it is going hazy around the edges. You get what you pay for.||||reg||1
Z||000010||88formula||08-11-2000||08:26 PM||||If you have glass coverage on your insurance than take it to a glass place and tell then a rock hit it. This way you will get a new windshield for free. Works for me!||||reg||1
Z||000011||fierodave||08-11-2000||10:12 PM||||Triumph auto glass~~~ there a national CO.  they install mine for $135.00 tax and molding included.<BR>and have NEVER seen a bad one yet from them!  the guys here local to me were the only ones that didn't say "OH a Fiero"  and they actually liked all the ones I have had done there(14 so far)<BR>just do a search for Triumph auto glass  or Diamond Glass co.<BR>they have  1-800 numbers.<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://members.theglobe.com/fierodave/gifs/fierosig.gif">  <p>[This message has been edited by fierodave (edited 08-11-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000012||dman||08-11-2000||11:17 PM||||Hello everyone. This talk of windshields has me very curious. I've already done a search on the forum and haven't found this information thus far.<P>How exactly do you replace a windshield? What are the steps required. Can the molding be reused? How do you take it off without tearing it up? Where do you get the adhesive?<P>I've never done it before and I've got a parts car that I can use for the donor. Yeah, I could probably find someone to replace it for $130 complete, but this is something I want to do myself.<P>To those who have done this before, any advice, instructions, or references would be greatly appreciated.<P>Thanks in advance!<P>||||reg||1
